 "phase_cost_share_at_current_deploy": {
  "advisory_56pct_reconciliation": "the 2026-08-28 advisory's 'early ~56% of arbiter cost' is the r_from_plies (playout-LENGTH) model. The PREREG-mandated fallback (r_from_secs, fired because the two models disagree 35.6% > 15%) puts early at share_PRIMARY_r_from_secs. Mechanism: early playouts are ~1.68x LONGER but each ply runs on a SMALLER board, so measured worker-seconds scale by only ~1.27x. Both are printed; the seconds model is the one with a stopwatch behind it and is the CONSERVATIVE one for the gate proposal.",
  "note": "share_if_r_ignored is the fires-only share, printed so the two mechanisms (more fires vs costlier playouts) stay separable",
