  "three_model_note": "r_from_plies is the ADVISORY's model and is REFUTED by two independent cost measurements: this package's contended per-record seconds (rung3_r5, n=6,602) and the exclusive-tenant sequential profile (PROFILE_TIER1.md section 3, n=480, identity-gated). Both say cost is NOT proportional to remaining plies -- per-ply cost rises ~1.8x as the board fills, so the long early playouts run on cheap small boards. The two measured models agree on the early share to within 1 percentage point; the ply model over-states it by ~14 points.",
